# rfc-004-watch-tracking.mdc

## Title
RFC 004 – Video Watch Tracking & Progress

## Summary
This RFC defines the mechanism for tracking users' video viewing activity and calculating their progress across courses. It enables fine-grained progress tracking and visibility for users, team leads, and admins.

---

## Goals
- Log watch duration per video and user
- Mark videos as completed when fully watched
- Use watch logs to calculate course progress
- Display real-time progress indicators in UI

## Database Tables
### `watch_logs`
| Field        | Type      | Description                        |
|--------------|-----------|------------------------------------|
| id           | uuid      | Primary key                        |
| user_id      | uuid      | FK to profiles                     |
| video_id     | uuid      | FK to videos                       |
| watched_time | interval  | Duration of time watched           |
| completed    | boolean   | Whether the video is completed     |
| updated_at   | timestamp | Last updated                       |

## Frontend Behavior
- Automatically log video watch activity using JS events
- Update watched duration in intervals (e.g., every 30s)
- Mark video as complete when duration >= 90% of total length
- Show completion checkmark and progress bar
- Course progress = completed videos / total videos

## Role Visibility
- **User**: Sees own progress
- **Team Lead/Admin**: View progress of assigned users
- **Guest**: No tracking

## UX Elements
- Progress bar in course cards and course detail
- Checkmarks on completed videos
- Resume where you left off (optional Phase 2)

## Validation Rules
- Prevent fake progress updates (e.g., skipping entire video)
- Backend must verify total duration vs watched duration

## Timeline
**Sprint 4**
- Create `watch_logs` table
- Add client-side tracking logic with debounced API calls
- Implement progress calculation per course

